{"id": "EUVD-2026-80548", "enisaUuid": "b86eb18f-4fca-3626-b5b0-011d068e974a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbatman-adv: bla: fix freeing of claims on meshif deletion\n\nWhen the mesh interface is getting deleted, then\nbatadv_bla_del_backbone_claims() (via batadv_bla_purge_backbone_gw()) could\nmake sure that all claims gets removed. But this function is only executed\nwhen bat_priv->bla.claim_hash is not NULL. And since batadv_bla_free() is\nalways setting it to NULL before it is (indirectly) called, it was never\nactually executed.\n\nBut the batadv_bla_purge_claims() -> batadv_handle_unclaim() is at the\nmoment too fragile because the BLA code is not handling the rehashing in\nbatadv_bla_update_orig_address(). The stored backbone address doesn't have\nto be the one actually used for the hash bucket selection during the\ninitial adding of the backbone. The batadv_handle_unclaim() can therefore\nfail to find the respective backbone for the unclaim and then stop the\ndeletion.\n\nBut the actual backbone_gw object is not needed for the unclaim because all\nrelevant information is always provided by the caller. And the check for\nthe existence of the backbone_gw doesn't provide any additional security\ncheck for the deletion of a claim.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:32:34", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:55:22", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/844a95a734f178d56c7acce14c5cce2cecff7e1a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/baeb1a28fd8e2f68193650d3664a8cd1adfd85c6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aacffa780a37e06cd5a13d33740a6e96c3a67e6c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/76aedcde5a2489cc971d4d1e396e784a49565e96", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f50edb69082a8ba990cc23d642089829f99afe6a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/871acdf97f64cee8398f72b88b89e8b4f4816dbe", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9a0c47023d3254048a1588534755d4476bcc3abc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8d128c932bced74e3b1625ba3d7c78ef122a88a7"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89948", "GHSA-9m5r-cr5m-2hhr"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "16e44673-8c13-3475-a06c-5168cdf9c385", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "23721387c409087fd3b97e274f34d3ddc0970b74 <f50edb69082a8ba990cc23d642089829f99afe6a"}, {"id": "17c51bdc-c63d-3635-af61-2a615140661b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "23721387c409087fd3b97e274f34d3ddc0970b74 <871acdf97f64cee8398f72b88b89e8b4f4816dbe"}, {"id": "26120c4b-db81-3fc9-a37b-867f7dcc5480", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "5dbeb342-4e94-3ef0-8227-5984e3c949cf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "23721387c409087fd3b97e274f34d3ddc0970b74 <aacffa780a37e06cd5a13d33740a6e96c3a67e6c"}, {"id": "672cb584-6584-355f-91df-bbda56cf225e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "7d3c6727-039a-38b8-838c-37eefaa71b37", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "86161e3a-5ba3-3500-8ff6-3eacaf1cda7f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.221"}, {"id": "87f351ba-ba49-32be-835c-67b0c7920b03", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.270"}, {"id": "a6d49e4c-625f-342c-a75a-b6ad65e0c15c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "23721387c409087fd3b97e274f34d3ddc0970b74 <8d128c932bced74e3b1625ba3d7c78ef122a88a7"}, {"id": "a907f758-e916-3186-b03d-9a301e2e9939", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "23721387c409087fd3b97e274f34d3ddc0970b74 <baeb1a28fd8e2f68193650d3664a8cd1adfd85c6"}, {"id": "ab0ef352-c6d5-3fbe-a6d6-e4b9c095aa12", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendo